      "message": "silentpayments: reject label tweaks that overflow the group order\n\nPreviously, a label tweak returned by the `label_lookup` callback that\nis not smaller than the group order was silently reduced modulo the\ngroup order. Such a tweak can never be produced by\n`secp256k1_silentpayments_recipient_label_create`, so it indicates a\ncorrupted or improperly constructed label cache, i.e., a bug on the\ncaller side rather than invalid data from an untrusted source. Treat\nthis as an API misuse (similar to the magic byte checks on the\n`prevouts_summary` argument), document the requirement, and add a\ntest.\n\nThe assignment of the found output is moved after the label tweak\ncheck, so that the found_outputs[k] entry is left untouched if the\nscan is aborted due to an invalid label tweak.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Sebastian Falbesoner",
        "email": "sebastian.falbesoner@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-22T02:56:00Z"
