      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "tACK b5fb2adf090d49b034db86b60a740d6058743ff7\n\nI built the head with CMake on macOS arm64 and ran ctest: all 231 tests pass. I also wrote a small program against the public API that scans a one-output labeled transaction with several tweaks in the label cache, and ran it against the head and the merge base. With the tweak from `recipient_label_create`, both find the output and return a tweak that spends it. With the group order or 2^256-1, the merge base returns 1 and a tweak that does not spend the output. The head calls the illegal callback, returns 0, reports no found outputs and leaves the found-output entry untouched. I can share the program if useful.\n",
